{
  "description": "When native interleaving is requested the renderer reconciles the two views by counting interpreter evaluation frames against call-entry Python frames. With an older interpreter the evaluation frame is recognized from a different symbol; a successful match interleaves the stacks, while a count mismatch falls back to the unable-to-merge notice followed by a plain listing of any Python frames.",
